While the canchoke check[1] is not performed with tins, it's still
unlikely to choke on them if you are were not satiated. As Daniel
pointed out, this implies uhunger_beforetin < 1000 (not satiated) and
uhunger_aftertin >= 2000 (choked) which is impossible. The other
alternative (if we don't look behind the keyboard) would be a
bug--perhaps in one of the "angry fruitsalad"-patches, more probably
somewhere else.

[1] Usually, a field canchoke is set to true for every victual at the
beginning of eating, if and only if your character was satiated
(uhunger>=1000) at that time.


